+// sysctl debug.wexdmc / debug.wexdc (2026-11-14): the correct display microcontroller program for Tiger Lake.
+//  Apple's kext carries an Ice Lake-lineage DMC (first word 0x0b004040) and, with dc6config=0, loads none. Writing
+//  debug.wexdmc=1 loads Intel's tgl_dmc 2.12 main program (Linux intel_dmc_load_program order: payload to 0x80000..,
+//  the header's MMIO pairs, DC_STATE_DEBUG memory-up mask) while DC_STATE_EN is 0 and power well 1 is up. Nothing
+//  enters a DC state because of the load alone.
+//  debug.wexdc=1|2 writes DC_STATE_EN "up to DC5" / "up to DC6" and is refused unless the program was loaded here and
+//  pipe A is disabled (display off). debug.wexdc=0 clears it the way Linux gen9_write_dc_state does (rewrite until it
+//  reads back) and waits for power well 1, the CDCLK PLL lock and DBUF slice 1. Any display-path hook (AUX, link
+//  training, enablePipe, disableDisplay) clears it first. "WhateverXeDcStat" reports what was seen.
+#include "kern_tgl_dmc212.hpp"
+static volatile uint32_t wexDmcLoaded, wexDcArmed;
+static uint64_t wexDcStat[16];
+static void wexDcOff(uint32_t why) {
