+// sysctl debug.wexl1ss (2026-11-14): PCIe L1 PM substates for the PCH root ports the firmware left at L1 only.
+//  bit 0 = RP04 (0:1C.0) + SD card reader, bit 1 = RP09 (0:1D.0) + NVMe. Writing the mask programs the pairs whose bit
+//  is set and clears the substates of the others, in the Linux pcie_aspm order: ASPM L1 off on the endpoint then the
+//  port, L1.2 enables off, T_POWER_ON and common-mode restore time (the larger of both ends), LTR_L1.2_THRESHOLD,
+//  enables on the port then the endpoint, ASPM L1 back on. Nothing is written until the sysctl is written; a reboot
+//  returns to the firmware state. "WhateverXeL1ssStat": per pair cap/ctl before and after.
+static int wexL1ss = 0;
