+static int wexDepopClamp(int v) { return v < 0 ? 0 : (v > 500 ? 500 : v); }
+// Headset CTIA coefficients in the driver (2026-11-15, replaces the user agent local.headset-ctia). With a headset in the
+// combo jack (pin 0x21 presence) the ALC257 vendor coefficients 0x45 and 0x1B (node 0x20) must read 0xD489 and 0x0C2B,
+// otherwise the earphones crackle; they come back with other values after codec power-up or a re-plug. A check runs
+// 300 ms after the function group is powered to D0 and after the driver sees the jack become occupied, and any write the
+// driver itself makes to those two coefficients while the jack is occupied is replaced by the headset value.
+// Coefficient verbs are the 4-bit forms SET_COEF_INDEX 0x5, SET_PROC_COEF 0x4, GET_PROC_COEF 0xC: IOHDACodecDevice::
+// executeVerb sends a verb below 0x10 as verb<<16 | 16-bit payload, anything else as verb<<8 | (payload & 0xFF), so the
+// 12-bit spellings 0x500/0x400 cut the value to its low byte (2026-11-15: 0xD489 went in as 0x0089, 0x0C2B as 0x002B,
